{"id":"ccbd3837-198f-4648-99b1-0eff5166b62b","object":"chat.completion","created":1793869883,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Now I have all three mechanisms. Applying scoped edits to all three files.\n\n```python\nenv_old1 = '''    @staticmethod\n    def int_or_none() -> EnvVar[int | None]:\n        return EnvVar(lambda v: int(v) if v is not None else None)\n'''\nenv_new1 = '''    @staticmethod\n    def int_or_none() -> EnvVar[int | None]:\n        return EnvVar(lambda v: int(v) if v is not None else None)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def int_or_none_min(*, minimum: int) -> EnvVar[int | None]:\n        \"\"\"未设置时为 None；设置时必须能按 int 解析且不小于 minimum。\"\"\"\n\n        def _init(v: str | None) -> int | None:\n            if v is None:\n                return None\n            value = int(v)\n            if value < minimum:\n                raise ValueError(f\"{value}, must be >= {minimum}\")\n            return value\n\n        return EnvVar(_init)\n'''\n\nenv_old2 = '''    # -- Logging --\n    DEEPINFER_LOGGING_INTERVAL_STEP = EnvVar.int(default=100)\n'''\nenv_new2 = '''    # -- Logging --\n    DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar.int_or_none_min(minimum=32)\n    \"\"\"普通诊断日志消息正文的最大字符数：未设置表示不限长；设置时须为 >= 32 的\n    整数，否则抛出 ValueError。统计日志通过 keep_full_message 不受该预算限制。\"\"\"\n    DEEPINFER_LOGGING_INTERVAL_STEP = EnvVar.int(default=100)\n'''\n\nprint(replace_text_batch(\"deepinfer/environ.py\", [{\"old_text\": env_old1, \"new_text\": env_new1}, {\"old_text\": env_old2, \"new_text\": env_new2}], \"fe2c531989c419f0b51b169a07f5ed826dcec7f95c0c5bc3a351805923c4f218\"))\n```","reasoning_content":"I have the mechanisms. Now let me check how DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS should be read in logger.py — need to import envs? Let's check whether envs is accessible; logger.py doesn't import environ. Check environ imports — environ.py imports nothing from logger (my search failed but environ.py top shows no import of logger; actually the search errored). environ.py doesn't import logger (it's standalone config). logger.py importing environ may create circular import? environ.py imports os, threading, collections.abc, datetime, typing — no deepinfer imports. So logger.py can import environ safely... but environ.py imports nothing from deepinfer, so `from deepinfer.environ import envs` in logger.py is safe.\n\nBut wait: logger.py is imported by environ? No. Good.\n\nAlternatively read env var lazily inside _setup_logger via envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS. But that requires envs. Let's do a lazy import inside function to be safe.\n\nNow write environ edit: add a factory `int_or_none_min` or add helper. Requirement: unset -> None; set -> int parse, must be >= 32; empty string, unparsable, or <32 -> ValueError containing var name. Note empty string: int(\"\") raises ValueError. Error message must contain the variable name — the descriptor's __get__ wraps exceptions with f\"{self.name}: {e}\". Good, so ValueError from init gets prefixed with name.\n\nCareful: __get__ catches Exception e, then `raise type(e)(f\"{self.name}: {e}\") from e` — inside try, if TypeError occurs (e.g. ValueError constructed with one arg is fine), then raise e from None. ValueError with one string arg works fine.\n\nAdd factory method to EnvVar:\n\n```python\n    @staticmethod\n    def int_or_none_at_least(minimum: int) -> EnvVar[int | None]:\n        def _init(v: str | None) -> int | None:\n            if v is None:\n                return None\n            value = int(v)\n            if value < minimum:\n                raise ValueError(f\"{value}, must be >= {minimum}\")\n            return value\n        return EnvVar(_init)\n```\n\nHmm, name-mangled? No. Adding a new factory method is allowed (\"描述符类可以新增辅助工厂方法\").\n\nThen add in envs:\n```python\n    DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar.int_or_none_at_least(32)\n    \"\"\"普通诊断日志消息正文的最大字符数；未设置表示不限长；设置时须为 >=32 的整数。\"\"\"\n```\nPlace it in the Logging section.\n\nNow logger.py: extend NewLineFormatter with max_message_chars keyword-only.\n\nImplementation:\n\n```python\n_MESSAGE_OMITTED = \"...<omitted>...\"\n_MESSAGE_MIN_BUDGET = 32\n\n\nclass NewLineFormatter(logging.Formatter):\n    def __init__(self, fmt, datefmt=None, high_precision=False, use_color=False, *, max_message_chars=None):\n        super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n        if max_message_chars is not None:\n            if isinstance(max_message_chars, bool) or not isinstance(max_message_chars, int):\n                raise ValueError(f\"max_message_chars must be an int >= {_MESSAGE_MIN_BUDGET} or None, got {max_message_chars!r}\")\n            if max_message_chars < _MESSAGE_MIN_BUDGET:\n                raise ValueError(...)\n        self.max_message_chars = max_message_chars\n```\n\nThen format:\n\n```python\n    def format(self, record):\n        if self.max_message_chars is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True:\n            record.message = record.getMessage()\n            record.message = self._truncate(record.message)\n            # need to build msg without recomputing message\n            ...\n```\n\nTricky: super().format(record) computes record.message = record.getMessage() and uses it. To avoid mutating record (msg, args, exc_info, stack_info must not be changed — mutating record.message is probably acceptable? The spec says can't rewrite shared record's msg, args, exc_info, stack_info. record.message is derived. But other handlers later compute their own message anyway. Safer: compute the truncated message locally and format manually.\n\nApproach: temporarily set record.message? That mutates. Alternative: build prefix/suffix ourselves? Better approach: use a copy of the record? copy module is not in allowed imports... for my own agent code, not the target code. Target source code can import whatever (it's business source; allowed to add imports). But copying a LogRecord is fiddly.\n\nCleaner: use a helper that computes the full formatted string with truncated message:\n\n```python\n    def format(self, record):\n        budget = self.max_message_chars\n        if budget is None or getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is True:\n            return self._format_with_message(record, None)\n        return self._format_with_message(record, budget)\n```\n\nHmm, simpler: implement via a saved/restored `record.message`... but super().format sets record.message itself.\n\nAlternative trick: override format by computing message ourselves and applying truncation to the final string's message portion. The formatter output format is fmt with %(message)s. The prefix/suffix could contain the message-derived text? Prefix is fixed (level, time, filename, lineno). The rule says budget limits message body, not prefix/traceback/stack_info. So one approach: format normally, then find the message substring in the result and replace it. That's fragile if message appears in prefix.\n\nBetter approach: compute `message = record.getMessage()`, truncate, then format using a lightweight record proxy. Standard trick used in vLLM-ish code:\n\n```python\ndef format(self, record):\n    ...\n    record.message = ...\n```\nActually logging.Formatter.format:\n\n```python\n    def format(self, record):\n        record.message = record.getMessage()\n        if self.usesTime():\n            record.asctime = self.formatTime(record, self.datefmt)\n        s = self.formatMessage(record)\n        if record.exc_info:\n            ...\n        if record.stack_info:\n            s = s + self.formatStack(record.stack_info)\n        return s\n```\n\nSo I can do: set record.message = truncated message, then call formatMessage-ish... The cleanest safe approach: use a shallow copy via a small wrapper object. But LogRecord copy: we could use `logging.makeLogRecord(record.__dict__)`? That creates a new LogRecord copying dict — that's clean and doesn't touch the original. logging.makeLogRecord(record.__dict__) copies attributes including msg, args, exc_info. Then set the copy's message. But then exc_text handling: formatter caches record.exc_text; ok.\n\nHowever, base Formatter.format sets record.message on the copy, fine.\n\nBut careful: formatTime conversions, usesTime etc. all fine on copy.\n\nSimplest and safe:\n\n```python\n    def format(self, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str:\n        if self.max_message_chars is None or getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is True:\n            return self._format_record(record)\n        ...\n```\nHmm, let me write:\n\n```python\n    def format(self, record):\n        source = record\n        if self.max_message_chars is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True:\n            source = self._with_truncated_message(record)\n        return self._format_message_record(source)\n\n    def _with_truncated_message(self, record):\n        message = record.getMessage()\n        truncated = _truncate_message(message, self.max_message_chars)\n        if truncated is message:\n            return record\n        proxy = logging.makeLogRecord(record.__dict__)\n        proxy.msg = truncated\n        proxy.args = ()\n        return proxy\n```\n\nWait: setting proxy.msg = truncated and args = () keeps proxy.getMessage() == truncated. Original record untouched. \n\nBut careful: record.exc_text caching and record.message on proxy - fine.\n\nDoes makeLogRecord exist? logging.makeLogRecord(dict) - yes, it's a module-level function.\n\nHmm, but exception text formatting: super().format(proxy) uses proxy.exc_info. Good. And `record.stack_info`. Good.\n\nBut one more consideration: for the multi-line prefix handling, existing format code uses record.message after super().format. I'll restructure:\n\n```python\n    def format(self, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str:\n        target = record\n        if self.max_message_chars is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True:\n            target = _truncated_record(record, self.max_message_chars)\n        msg = super().format(target)\n        if \"\\n\" in msg and target.message:\n            prefix = msg[: msg.find(target.message)]\n            msg = msg.replace(\"\\n\", \"\\n\" + prefix)\n        if self.use_color:\n            ...\n        return msg\n```\n\nNote original used `record.message`; using target.message is equivalent for untruncated case.\n\nTruncation function:\n\n```python\ndef _truncate_message(message: str, budget: int) -> str:\n    if len(message) <= budget:\n        return message\n    marker = _MESSAGE_OMITTED  # 15 chars\n    keep = budget - len(marker)\n    if keep <= 0:\n        return message  # budget guarantees >=32 so unreachable\n    head = (keep + 1) // 2\n    tail = keep - head\n    return f\"{message[:head]}{marker}{message[len(message) - tail:] if tail else ''}\"\n```\n\nCheck example: budget 32, marker 15 -> keep 17, head 9, tail 8. Requirement says \"预算32时，保留开头9字符、末尾8字符，加上15字符标记\" — yes, ceil(17/2)=9. Good.\n\nEdge: tail = 0 -> message[len-0:] = message[:]... careful! message[-0:] == message[0:] == whole string. So handle tail==0 with slice message[len(message):] => \"\". My expression uses `message[len(message) - tail:]` which for tail=0 gives message[len:] = \"\". Good.\n\nNow `_setup_logger`: read config value and pass it:\n\n```python\n    max_message_chars = _log_max_message_chars()\n    fmt = NewLineFormatter(_FORMAT, datefmt=_DATE_FORMAT, use_color=sys.stdout.isatty(), max_message_chars=max_message_chars)\n```\n\nHelper:\n```python\ndef _log_max_message_chars() -> int | None:\n    try:\n        from deepinfer.environ import envs\n    except Exception:  # pragma: no cover\n        return None\n    return envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS\n```\nHmm, importing inside function so environ env caching works. But wait, environ.py's envs class - accessing attribute triggers descriptor. Good.\n\nActually is there risk of a cycle: deepinfer/__init__.py imports? Let's check whether deepinfer/environ.py imports anything from deepinfer... The top-30 lines shown: no deepinfer imports beyond none. And does deepinfer/__init__.py import logger? If environ is imported by logger at module level, and __init__ imports logger... use lazy import to be safe. But careful with sys.modules: if logger is imported while environ is being imported (environ doesn't import logger). Fine.\n\nAlso, does importing deepinfer.environ import torch etc.? No.\n\nNow stats_logger: `logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})`.\n\nWait — but the workers in tests extract `_log_worker` from source. Line: `logger.info(m)` -> `logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})`.\n\nNow check the tests expectations for logger init: \"重复初始化不能重复添加处理器\" — existing code handles.\n\nAlso: does _setup_logger get called at import and again possibly on rearm? Test likely: set env, rearm, call init? Task says \"重新执行默认日志初始化时\" — maybe test calls `logger_module._setup_logger()`. Fine either way.\n\nLet me also double-check whether EnvVar's `__get__` wraps ValueError correctly and the message contains var name. Yes.\n\nOne more consideration: `int_or_none_at_least` — maybe better to name it something clearer: `int_or_none_min`. Fine.\n\nAlso empty string: `int(\"\")` -> ValueError(\"invalid literal for int() with base 10: ''\") → wrapped with name prefix. Good.\n\nLet's write the edits now. Need file hashes: environ fe2c..., logger 5b8f..., stats 9ef9....\n\nI'll use replace_text_batch for each file.\n\nFor logger.py, need to check current format lines exactly. From evidence ev-30754515034e43628968 lines 33-68 - full class. Good.\n\nEdits for logger.py:\n1. Insert helper functions before class? Add after `_COLOR_RESET = \"\\033[0m\"` block plus `_MESSAGE_OMITTED` constants. Actually insert constants near _COLOR_RESET:\n\nold:\n```\n_COLOR_RESET = \"\\033[0m\"\n```\nnew:\n```\n_COLOR_RESET = \"\\033[0m\"\n\n# 普通诊断日志消息正文的最小/默认截断预算与中间省略标记\n_MESSAGE_OMITTED = \"...<omitted>...\"\n_MIN_MESSAGE_CHARS = 32\n```\n\n2. Class __init__ replacement.\n3. format replacement + helper functions.\n4. _setup_logger fmt.\n\nLet me write them carefully with exact old text from evidence.\n\n__init__ old text (lines 29-39 approx):\n```\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        fmt: str,\n        datefmt: str | None = None,\n        high_precision: bool = False,\n        use_color: bool = False,\n    ) -> None:\n        super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n        self.high_precision = high_precision\n        self.use_color = use_color\n```\n\nNew:\n```\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        fmt: str,\n        datefmt: str | None = None,\n        high_precision: bool = False,\n        use_color: bool = False,\n        *,\n        max_message_chars: int | None = None,\n    ) -> None:\n        super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n        if max_message_chars is not None:\n            if isinstance(max_message_chars, bool) or not isinstance(max_message_chars, int):\n                raise ValueError(f\"max_message_chars must be an int >= {_MIN_MESSAGE_CHARS} or None, got {max_message_chars!r}\")\n            if max_message_chars < _MIN_MESSAGE_CHARS:\n                raise ValueError(f\"max_message_chars must be >= {_MIN_MESSAGE_CHARS}, got {max_message_chars}\")\n        self.high_precision = high_precision\n        self.use_color = use_color\n        self.max_message_chars = max_message_chars\n```\n\nformat old:\n```\n    def format(self, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str:\n        msg = super().format(record)\n        # 快速路径：单行日志（绝大多数情况）无需做对齐处理\n        if \"\\n\" in msg and record.message:\n            prefix = msg[: msg.find(record.message)]\n            msg = msg.replace(\"\\n\", \"\\n\" + prefix)\n        if self.use_color:\n            color = _LEVEL_COLORS.get(record.levelno)\n            if color:\n                msg = f\"{color}{msg}{_COLOR_RESET}\"\n        return msg\n```\n\nNew:\n```\n    def format(self, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str:\n        target = record\n        if self.max_message_chars is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True:\n            target = _truncated_record(record, self.max_message_chars)\n        msg = super().format(target)\n        # 快速路径：单行日志（绝大多数情况）无需做对齐处理\n        if \"\\n\" in msg and target.message:\n            prefix = msg[: msg.find(target.message)]\n            msg = msg.replace(\"\\n\", \"\\n\" + prefix)\n        if self.use_color:\n            color = _LEVEL_COLORS.get(record.levelno)\n            if color:\n                msg = f\"{color}{msg}{_COLOR_RESET}\"\n        return msg\n```\n\nNote: if truncated record's message appears also... fine.\n\nHmm one subtlety: `msg.find(target.message)` — if truncated message contains the marker... fine.\n\nAlso add module-level helpers `_truncate_message` and `_truncated_record` before the class. Insert into the constants edit block? Better insert after `_MIN_MESSAGE_CHARS` block... but functions should come after constants. Insert them right before `class NewLineFormatter`. I'll combine: put helper funcs in the class-insertion edit anchored on \"class NewLineFormatter(logging.Formatter):\".\n\nAnchor old text: `class NewLineFormatter(logging.Formatter):` → new: helpers + class line. But careful uniqueness: the class line appears once. Also `logger = ...`? fine.\n\nNote: `_truncated_record` uses logging.makeLogRecord.\n\nLet me write helper:\n\n```python\ndef _truncate_message(message: str, budget: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"按预算截断消息正文，中间用固定标记替换，标记计入预算。\"\"\"\n    if len(message) <= budget:\n        return message\n    keep = budget - len(_MESSAGE_OMITTED)\n    if keep <= 0:\n        return message\n    head = (keep + 1) // 2\n    tail = keep - head\n    return f\"{message[:head]}{_MESSAGE_OMITTED}{message[len(message) - tail:]}\"\n\n\ndef _truncated_record(record: logging.LogRecord, budget: int) -> logging.LogRecord:\n    \"\"\"返回带截断消息的记录副本，避免改动共享 LogRecord 的 msg/args 等字段。\"\"\"\n    message = record.getMessage()\n    truncated = _truncate_message(message, budget)\n    if truncated == message:\n        return record\n    proxy = logging.makeLogRecord(record.__dict__)\n    proxy.msg = truncated\n    proxy.args = ()\n    return proxy\n```\n\nCareful: truncated == message but different object? Only equal when not truncated. Fine.\n\nHmm, if truncated == message (no change) return record. If equal but we want? fine.\n\nAlso `proxy.args = ()` and msg=truncated; getMessage returns msg % args → no % in msg? If truncated message contains '%' (e.g. from a literal %s in args), then `msg % ()` raises ValueError \"not enough arguments\"? Actually \"%s\" % () raises TypeError: not enough arguments for format string. Yes! record.getMessage() = msg % args. If original message contains literal \"%\" from args substitution: e.g. msg=\"100%% done\" args=() → but if the formatted output contains a single \"%\", then applying % () again would fail.\n\nSafer: set proxy.msg = truncated and proxy.args = None? getMessage: \n```python\n    def getMessage(self):\n        msg = str(self.msg)\n        if self.args:\n            msg = msg % self.args\n        return msg\n```\nargs = () is falsy → ok! Empty tuple is falsy, so no % applied. Great, `()` is safe.\n\nBut then Formatter.format sets record.message = record.getMessage() = truncated. Good.\n\nHowever, proxy = makeLogRecord(record.__dict__) copies exc_text if set etc. Fine.\n\nAlso, `record.exc_info` shared - fine, not modified.\n\nOne risk: super().format(record) internally may set record.exc_text (caching) — on proxy, ok.\n\nNow _setup_logger:\n\nold:\n```\n    fmt = NewLineFormatter(\n        _FORMAT,\n        datefmt=_DATE_FORMAT,\n        use_color=sys.stdout.isatty(),\n    )\n```\nnew:\n```\n    fmt = NewLineFormatter(\n        _FORMAT,\n        datefmt=_DATE_FORMAT,\n        use_color=sys.stdout.isatty(),\n        max_message_chars=_log_max_message_chars(),\n    )\n```\n\nAnd add helper function `_log_max_message_chars` before _setup_logger (after `_default_handler = None`? Insert in the constants block region). I'll add it in the constants edit block after _MIN_MESSAGE_CHARS.\n\n```python\ndef _log_max_message_chars() -> int | None:\n    \"\"\"读取集中配置中的普通日志消息长度预算；未设置时返回 None（不限长）。\"\"\"\n    from deepinfer.environ import envs\n\n    return envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS\n```\n\nCircular import risk at module import time: _setup_logger() runs at import of logger, calling _log_max_message_chars → imports deepinfer.environ. If deepinfer/__init__ imports logger before environ... environ doesn't import logger, so fine.\n\nBut what if environ's module fails to import (e.g. missing deps)? It imports only stdlib. Good.\n\nLet me combine edits now. The constants block edit includes _MESSAGE_OMITTED, _MIN_MESSAGE_CHARS, and _log_max_message_chars function.\n\nOrder inside file: constants right after _COLOR_RESET; the helper function placed before _root_logger definition — but _COLOR_RESET block appears before the class... Wait, order in file: _FORMAT, _DATE_FORMAT, colors, then class NewLineFormatter (line 33), then _root_logger at line 71. So constants block is before class. Putting _log_max_message_chars right after _COLOR_RESET is fine (function referenced later at runtime).\n\nOK. Now write environ edit.\n\nEdit 1 anchor (factory methods) — add new staticmethod after `str_or_none`/`int_or_none`. Use anchor:\n```\n    @staticmethod\n    def int_or_none() -> EnvVar[int | None]:\n        return EnvVar(lambda v: int(v) if v is not None else None)\n```\nnew: same + blank + new factory.\n\nEdit 2 anchor in Logging section:\n```\n    # -- Logging --\n    DEEPINFER_LOGGING_INTERVAL_STEP = EnvVar.int(default=100)\n```\nnew: add the new config after interval step? Better put right after `# -- Logging --` line:\n```\n    # -- Logging --\n    DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar.int_or_none_min(32)\n    \"\"\"普通诊断日志消息正文的最大字符数：未设置表示不限长；设置时须为\n    >= 32 的整数，否则抛出 ValueError。统计日志通过 keep_full_message 不受限制。\"\"\"\n    DEEPINFER_LOGGING_INTERVAL_STEP = EnvVar.int(default=100)\n```\n\nName the factory `int_or_none_min(*, minimum: int)`. Keyword-only fine; call with `EnvVar.int_or_none_min(minimum=32)`.\n\nstats_logger edit:\nold:\n```\n            for m in msgs:\n                logger.info(m)\n```\nnew:\n```\n            for m in msgs:\n                logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})\n```\n\nThen run pytest.\n\nAlso need run.log and patch.diff at end. Let's do edits first.\n\nApply three replace_text_batch calls."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9070,"completion_tokens":5544,"total_tokens":14614,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":4096},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":5094},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":4096,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":4974},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}